  "subject": "A late-evening radio weather-reader in Kowloon ends every forecast with 'bring a jacket' for one lone taxi-driver listener, until a man in a worn jacket turns up at the studio door.",
  "caption": "Cantonese 1970s TV-drama-theme folk-pop in the Sam Hui lineage. Steel-string acoustic guitar strummed in open chords, singing harmonica answering each phrase, soft string pad, brushed snare with upright bass walking. Dry 1970s studio room, tape warmth, close-miked guitar. Male warm baritone, relaxed storytelling delivery, melody clearly sung. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 96 BPM, G major. Warm, gently teasing mood. No electric guitar distortion, no synth pads, no autotune, no rap, no drum machine, no choir.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n夜晚七點半 我打開咪\n同全港講聲 聽日會變天\n有個的士佬 日日打嚟\n話佢喺油塘 等緊我開聲\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我從來冇問 過佢個名\n但佢次次 都聽得出\n\n[Chorus]\n帶件褸啦 今晚有風\n我對住咪 輕輕講一句\n成個香港 當我報天氣\n得你知道 係講畀你\n\n[Verse]\n佢話架車 冇暖氣\n收音機 就係佢個伴\n我話低溫 得十二度\n電話入面 笑咗一聲\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n今晚電話 靜晒\n我睇住 盞紅燈\n\n[Chorus]\n帶件褸啦 今晚有風\n我對住咪 大聲講一句\n如果你喺度 聽到呢句\n打嚟啦 同我講天氣\n\n[Verse]\n第二朝 有個阿伯\n企喺廣播室門口\n手挽住 件舊褸\n話佢而家 轉咗日更\n\n[Bridge]\n原來個人 冇把聲咁高\n佢遞我 一壺熱茶\n兩個人 企喺走廊笑\n\n[Chorus]\n帶件褸啦 聽日有雨\n我對住咪 同你講一句\n成個香港 當我報天氣\n今次 我見到你\n\n[Outro]\n帶件褸啦\n聽日見",
